{"content":[{"c":["ANAMMELECH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Deity associated with Adrammelech, who was worshiped by the people of Sepharvaim, whom the Assyrians relocated in Samaria after 722 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". Anammelech is evidently the Hebrew rendering of the designation for a Mesopotamian deity, Anu-melek, meaning “Anu is King.” Anu was the name of the chief god of Assyria, the sky god. The worship of this deity by the Sepharvites in Samaria included child sacrifice (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.17.31","r":"2Kgs.17.31","rawR":"2Kgs.17.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.17.31","value":"2Kgs.17.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 17:31"},"). It is not certain whether the burning of children in the Anu cult was brought from Sepharvaim or was an innovation when the Sepharvites came to Canaan."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Mesopotamia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Mesopotamia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Mesopotamia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mesopotamia"},"; ",{"href":"?item=SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Syria, Syrians"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Anammelech","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 17:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.17.31","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.17.31","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.17.31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"90eca77b930e15dc31f947ad6b735fcd91751eb4f70848c5dd47a424924e19ef","sourceItemName":"Anammelech","sourceItemOrder":330,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Anammelech","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Anammelech","title":"Anammelech","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}